  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways, all leading to the target Detroit 98. The first pathway involves the inhibition of K-252a, a tyrosine-protein kinase, which in turn targets Detroit 98. The second pathway links Oblonganoside C to SBK1, a serine/threonine-protein kinase, which is also targeted by Theasaponin E1, another compound that ultimately affects Detroit 98. The third pathway involves the direct targeting of Detroit 98 by Oblonganoside C through a complex, non-tyrosine-protein kinase mechanism. These findings suggest that Oblonganoside C may act through multiple distinct molecular mechanisms to influence the activity of Detroit 98, potentially through different signaling pathways. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Oblonganoside C and Detroit 98, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple target pathways indicates that the compound may have a broad impact on cellular processes, potentially through different molecular mechanisms.",
